# Extra values for automation/.env.example.
#
# Neither var appears in docker-compose.yaml — both are read by
# tools/export-n8n-workflows.sh, so the generator can't find them on its own.
#
# N8N_API_KEY: an n8n API key with read access, used to dump workflow
# definitions to automation/n8n-workflows/. Create one in n8n under
# Settings -> API. Read-only use; never needs write scope.
N8N_API_KEY=
# N8N_EXPORT_REWRITES: semicolon-separated from=to pairs, applied in order as
# plain string replacements, that turn host-specific paths and domains in the
# exported JSON into the placeholder tree this repo documents. Kept here rather
# than in the script so the public repo carries no host specifics. Leaving it
# empty is safe but not useful: the exporter's own scan refuses to write a
# workflow that still contains a real mount path, home path, private address,
# or token, so an unconfigured run exports nothing rather than leaking.
N8N_EXPORT_REWRITES=/your/toolkit/path=/opt/homelab; /scripts/= /opt/homelab/scripts/
